<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikolay Chkheidze</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864–1926</span> · Also known as Nikoloz Chkheidze</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikolay Chkheidze was a Georgian Menshevik leader who chaired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> Soviet in 1917. Returning to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, he chaired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a> of the Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic in 1918 and then the constituent assembly of the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. After the Soviet invasion of 1921 he went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikolay-chkheidze.jpg" alt="Nikolay Chkheidze" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Auguste Léon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1919_Nicolas_Tchkheidze.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
